---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Hyphos Consulting designs and builds integrated business software. We exist because most organizations are running on a patchwork of tools that the people in the middle absorb the cost of."
>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 sm:px-8 pt-20 sm:pt-28 pb-16">
    <div class="eyebrow mb-3">About</div>
    <h1 class="display text-4xl sm:text-5xl leading-tight text-ink-900">
      We build the software you should never have had to stitch together yourself.
    </h1>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 sm:px-8 pb-20 space-y-12 text-ink-700 leading-relaxed">
    <div>
      <h2 class="display text-2xl text-ink-900 mb-3">Why we exist</h2>
      <p>
        Most organizations are running on a tangle of point tools — a CRM here, a marketing platform there, a scheduling app, an email service, a billing system, a website, a separate analytics dashboard. Each one promised efficiency. None of them talk to each other. The people in the middle absorb the integration cost in their evenings, in their tab-switching, in their copy-paste.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4">
        Worse, the AI wave is now layering on top of that mess. Five new copilots, each with no memory of the others. Six different "agents" stuck inside six different products. The fragmentation problem doesn't go away — it accelerates.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4">
        Hyphos Consulting exists because someone has to build the integrated layer instead. That's what we do.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="display text-2xl text-ink-900 mb-3">What we believe</h2>
      <p>
        Software's job is to disappear. The best software fades into the background of the work, takes the manual coordination off your team's plate, and gives back the time that should have been spent on the part of the job people actually care about — the relationships, the judgment calls, the craft.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4">
        We don't believe in efficiency for its own sake. We've watched too many "transformation" projects optimize organizations into joyless machines. We believe in human flourishing — software that lets people do meaningful work at a sustainable pace, where relationships are characterized by loyalty and genuine care, where the most vulnerable people in your organization are protected, not sacrificed to aggregate optimization.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-ink-900">
        <strong>Efficiency is not the goal. Human flourishing is the goal.</strong> The efficiency falls out as a side effect.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="display text-2xl text-ink-900 mb-3">How we work</h2>
      <p>
        Small team, named lead, two-week shippable increments. We sit with your front-line people, not just your executives. We show working software early — not slide decks. We tell you when we think you shouldn't hire us, and we mean it.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4">
        We take on a few engagements a year, by design. The work is better when we can stay close to it.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="display text-2xl text-ink-900 mb-3">The Hyphos family</h2>
      <p>
        Hyphos Consulting is the services arm. We own and operate two pieces of software ourselves:
      </p>
      <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3">
        <li>
          <strong class="text-ink-900"><a href="/products#foundation" class="link">Foundation</a></strong> — our integrated business operating system (sixteen modules, one database) that we adapt to each industry. First deployment live; additional industries in scoping.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="text-ink-900"><a href="/products#hyphos" class="link">Hyphos</a></strong> — enterprise knowledge, learning, and apprenticeship on a persistent graph. In early access at <a href="https://hyphos.io" class="link">hyphos.io</a>.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-4">
        All of it operates under one premise: software that gets out of the way so people can focus on people.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="display text-2xl text-ink-900 mb-3">Talk to us</h2>
      <p>
        If any of this resonates — or if you've got a system that's quietly costing your team hours every week and you don't know where to start — <a href="/contact" class="link">start a conversation</a>. The first call is on us.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>
